      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village sprang to life in 1870 when the Union Pacific built a station house that doubled as post office, schoolhouse, and land office.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potter%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1928, Potter witnessed the largest hailstone ever recorded in the United States, measuring 17 inches across and weighing 1.5 pounds.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
